1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Hello world, I am Ayaan from India and this is OmniSearch.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,500
OmniSearch is a local file search engine built in Python,

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:14,500
unlike traditional file tools which search files on the basis of filenames.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,500
OmniSearch relies on the content and meaning of the files.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,000
When I run my project, it prompts you for three options: Store, Search, and Quit.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,500
When I press 0 and give it a path to a directory in my PC,

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,500
it will first load the OpenAI CLIP model into RAM.

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,500
Now what it does is index through every file in that folder

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,000
and convert it into a vector.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,500
Now what is a vector, you may ask?

11
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:50,000
A vector is a 1-dimensional array consisting of, in this case, 512 numbers.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,500
Files that have a similar vector will go to the same neighborhood in the space

13
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,500
which is created by the vector.

14
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,500
I have added support for various file types in this project.

15
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:11,000
In the case of a zip archive, it first inspects the archive in memory,

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
then creates a vector for a string containing the archive's name and internal files.

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
For PDFs, it indexes through every page and creates a vector of the text it contains.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,500
Here, let me show you this project running.

19
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:32,500
I have a directory called Documents in which I have folders and an image of a sunrise.

20
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:36,000
So now let me run this project.

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,500
After running, it asks for an option. I'll enter 0 to store and enter /home/ayaan/Documents.

22
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:48,500
You can see that 185 items were saved into the database from my directory.

23
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:54,000
Now when I select 1 to Search, there is a category filter: All, Images, PDFs, Code, and Text.

24
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,500
If I select Images (filter 1), it loads the AI model.

25
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:05,000
Now it asks me to enter the query for the file I am trying to search.

26
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
When I enter 'sunrise' as my query, I get the top results with match percentages.

27
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,500
If I open the first result, you can see the same image and the exact path right here.

28
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:22,500
So this is how my project works.

29
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:28,000
Now I will quit the program with 'q' and run pytest on test_project.py.

30
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:35,000
And you can see all tests passed! 3 passed in 0.23 seconds.

31
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:41,000
These are the unit tests for storing, opening, and filtering the database.

32
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Now I would like to thank David Malan and the whole CS50 team for this amazing course.

33
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
This was CS50!
